{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hdr image based lighting for cg hdr image based lighting for cg","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG.md","fileName":"HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CG Integration and Render Passes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CG Integration and Render Passes","Light Probe Reference for CG","Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hdr image based lighting for cg hdr image based lighting for cg","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG.md","fileName":"HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG","heading":"HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Image-based lighting uses the colors and intensities of an environment image to illuminate CG. A high-dynamic-range image retains exposure differences beyond those of an ordinary display image, so a bright sun region can contribute far more light than shaded surroundings even when the monitor cannot display that full range. The book distinguishes an HDRI from the global-illumination method that uses it: an image can be a lighting source without lighting the scene globally. See [[Light Probe Reference for CG]] and [[Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection]].","tags":["baby"],"link